course: dictionary
lesson: 15263
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things in different places. Context tells you which meaning is right. Look at the words around it: the topic, the subject, and the other words in the sentence.
explain: «The choir sang do, re, mi, fa, so, la, si.» Here si is a music note. The list is a musical scale, so the topic is music, and the note is the seventh one in that scale.
explain: «Scientists measure length in metres, which are SI units.» Here SI is a science word. Science talks about measuring, so SI must be the short name for a system of units, not a note.
explain: «Ana asked if we wanted to play, and she said, «¡Sí!»» Here sí is Spanish for yes. The exclamation mark and the question tell you it is a reply, not a note or a unit. When you are unsure, check the dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: The word si is a music note: in some countries it is the seventh note of do-re-mi, and in English it is usually called ti.
fact: SI stands for the International System of Units, from the French «Système international». Scientists use it for metres, kilograms and seconds.
fact: «Sí» is Spanish and means «yes». «Si» means «if» or «yes» in some other languages, and it is not an English word.
fact: Si is also a short nickname for the name Simon. Context will show you which meaning is meant.
exercise: «The choir sang do, re, mi, fa, so, la, si.» What is si in this sentence? | *The seventh note of the do-re-mi scale | A tall tower | The first word of a song | A kind of bird
exercise: «Scientists measure length in metres, which are SI units.» What does SI stand for? | Super Important | Science Inside | Simple Instructions | *The International System of Units
exercise: Ana from Madrid says «¡Sí!» when you ask her a question. What does sí mean? | Thank you | No | Hello | *Yes
test: Which of these is an SI unit used in science? | *Kilogram | Note | Yes | Simon
test: «Ana asked if we wanted to play, and she said, «¡Sí!»» What does sí mean here? | Goodbye | *Yes | A unit of length | A musical note
exam: In some countries the seventh note of the scale is called si; what is it called in English? | Fa | Re | *Ti | Do
